# Equinox does not counter a spell that would destroy a land only if a choice is made (rulings, CR 608.2): Cleansing
# destroys Bot1's enchanted Plains only unless a player pays 1 life, so it is not countered. Equinox's speculation tried
# paying on a hidden copy of the game only: no one's life changed, and the real Cleansing then asks for real - both save
# nothing, and every land is destroyed (Equinox, enchanting nothing, follows its Plains, CR 704.5m).

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Equinox
Plains x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Black Lotus
Cleansing
Plains x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Equinox.Cast(Plains)
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot2.Hand.Cleansing.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate(Stack.Cleansing; Ability: Counter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Life = 20
? Bot2.Life = 20
? Bot1.Battlefield = Equinox; Mox Pearl; Plains
Bot2.Choose()
Bot1.Choose()

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Pearl
Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 0
Bot2.Graveyard = Cleansing; Plains; Black Lotus
